{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:22:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_83e063e10e794567a685a4233f87a7c7","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_b6ef33a419da9b6a4754696182b48949da68678461ff6d67210f042d8e355858","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"neovateai/neovate-code@0a24b363ecbe snapshot d399a326a058e2ba","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_42d32d54fa0d11eb61c88032d8fdb9e40396dad0d8d84847a944fbc91a33423c","slc_e87317f40a6d7c92200faa23d8b6f62f16be30f5f0684b7fdfb39b84d89d4e9b"],"source_ids":["src_713f4f24bf0c550fb7498b9a778269e1"],"text":"A 2025-01-27 plan proposes background bash execution so the LLM can monitor and control long-running development tasks, extending the bash tool with a BackgroundTaskManager plus bash_output and kill_bash tools.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:22:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_83e063e10e794567a685a4233f87a7c7"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:22:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_83e063e10e794567a685a4233f87a7c7","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_c00023d751c7808ad2a8828b7712b7ae498a1f0ef28dae622d6a9fecbbcb21da","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"neovateai/neovate-code@0a24b363ecbe snapshot d399a326a058e2ba","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_abf5fc59b80b4530250c14304af8eee27388da853ec2af1376e14525be35d27d","slc_cab6fdf6517ed7375f1e74d80b0d2a94cc58da44810a38f4a58055e4c56b37e7"],"source_ids":["src_7777df607ea65d5789c4cc37024ef061"],"text":"A design doc dated 2025-01-26 addresses terminal focus escape sequences ([I]/[O]) appearing as literal text in the chat input when modals are shown, because Ink strips the escape prefix.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:22:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_83e063e10e794567a685a4233f87a7c7"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:22:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_83e063e10e794567a685a4233f87a7c7","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_cbf9163feda76f637f22834f0145cccd52552d5ab51967614e85160c15d985a1","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"neovateai/neovate-code@0a24b363ecbe snapshot d399a326a058e2ba","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_bf52c930d0f8c4dcc541176f96a8295ebeff1957a39844b1580941d858c03c6b","slc_ebeb8a5df8f88656da13a5615c705740045b36ba8c61209782152998f8ea0db5"],"source_ids":["src_713f4f24bf0c550fb7498b9a778269e1"],"text":"The plan adds a run_in_background boolean parameter to the bash tool and documents that dev-pattern commands auto-move to background after 2 seconds if producing output, returning a task_id for bash_output and kill_bash.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:22:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_83e063e10e794567a685a4233f87a7c7"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:22:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_83e063e10e794567a685a4233f87a7c7","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_dde1f11e32a47a9519330fb4b72cd4f5db5114039e8d2fce8f5d25c6f58519c2","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"neovateai/neovate-code@0a24b363ecbe snapshot d399a326a058e2ba","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3b7c0ed0905a2127d99433e35daf549b55b1232c94127cbe5521c351298db60c","slc_4d5e117792dd1dda45564f1208d45086ec0bb47d17a967c33fd50e7ec2477fe9"],"source_ids":["src_713f4f24bf0c550fb7498b9a778269e1"],"text":"In the planned design, bash_output requires no approval (category 'read', needsApproval returns false), while kill_bash refuses to terminate tasks whose status is not 'running'.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:22:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_83e063e10e794567a685a4233f87a7c7"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:22:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_83e063e10e794567a685a4233f87a7c7","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_fc2956f870a29f84b57798055cc5fa63e7450eb920f6e4f6548956a723ea6134","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"neovateai/neovate-code@0a24b363ecbe snapshot d399a326a058e2ba","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1ad7465607521fbe038709104e82429396a3fe340579a62245fedc44c489c3c1","slc_a348e629c82b306e4218eba0c3cfc33c3a9535db9e3a801ebe92cb8774680910"],"source_ids":["src_713f4f24bf0c550fb7498b9a778269e1"],"text":"The planned killTask uses taskkill on Windows; otherwise it signals the process group with SIGTERM, then SIGKILL after 200ms if still running, falling back to killing the pid directly.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:22:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_83e063e10e794567a685a4233f87a7c7"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:22:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_83e063e10e794567a685a4233f87a7c7","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_fddc79e3507044a1182c9e093186a43a59186cc79f8ece553c42bc7f8f03b83c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"neovateai/neovate-code@0a24b363ecbe snapshot d399a326a058e2ba","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_c14b391b942dee185997ab01a3ef019955babe65af8b5376c96a81a4849ee884"],"source_ids":["src_7777df607ea65d5789c4cc37024ef061"],"text":"The focus handler updates window focus state via useAppStore.getState().setWindowFocused, setting true for '[I' (focus gained) and false for '[O' (focus lost).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:22:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_83e063e10e794567a685a4233f87a7c7"}
